WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:00:46.088 --> 00:00:50.468
Tal'Dorei's kingdoms
lay broken at my feet.

3
00:00:50.468 --> 00:00:53.971
yet my conclave continues to fail me.

4
00:00:53.971 --> 00:00:55.890
Send me. my king.

5
00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.642
I will dispatch those that threaten you.

6
00:00:58.642 --> 00:01:00.686
You have your talents.

7
00:01:00.686 --> 00:01:03.063
But with Umbrasyl fallen.

8
00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:07.276
Raishan's mission
is more crucial than ever.

9
00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:11.697
We are not alone.

10
00:01:19.705 --> 00:01:21.832
Something was here.

11
00:01:35.387 --> 00:01:36.806
What?

12
00:01:41.352 --> 00:01:42.978
Oh. gods.

13
00:01:42.978 --> 00:01:45.356
Yes.

14
00:01:45.356 --> 00:01:49.151
My children soon will be gods.

15
00:02:25.896 --> 00:02:27.064
No!

16
00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:40.202
{\an8}<i>Thordak is becoming irrational.</i>

17
00:02:40.202 --> 00:02:41.787
{\an8}<i>Insane.</i>

18
00:02:41.787 --> 00:02:44.957
Intent on stripping Tal'Dorei of its gold.

19
00:02:44.957 --> 00:02:47.835
But not to satisfy his greed.

20
00:02:47.835 --> 00:02:49.837
For another purpose.

21
00:02:49.837 --> 00:02:51.422
What purpose?

22
00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:54.800
- Enough of this yappin'!
- Grog. don't!

23
00:02:57.511 --> 00:02:58.637
Okay.

24
00:02:58.637 --> 00:03:00.180
Maybe a little more yappin'.

25
00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.976
Everyone in this chamber shares a goal.

26
00:03:03.976 --> 00:03:06.020
The end of the Cinder King.

27
00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:10.065
And if you join me. it is a goal
we are capable of achieving.

28
00:03:10.065 --> 00:03:13.319
We know firsthand what you're capable of.

29
00:03:13.319 --> 00:03:15.613
Your kind razed Byroden.

30
00:03:15.613 --> 00:03:18.282
Nearly everyone in our village dead.

31
00:03:18.282 --> 00:03:20.075
Including our mother.

32
00:03:20.075 --> 00:03:22.703
Not all dragons are the same.

33
00:03:22.703 --> 00:03:26.123
Some can be cruel.

34
00:03:26.123 --> 00:03:29.168
Some can be clever.

35
00:03:29.168 --> 00:03:31.712
But some can be truthful.

36
00:03:37.009 --> 00:03:40.179
Thordak did that to you?

37
00:03:40.179 --> 00:03:41.805
Not exactly.

38
00:03:41.805 --> 00:03:44.308
But he will be punished nonetheless.

39
00:03:44.308 --> 00:03:46.644
So it's revenge you're after.

40
00:03:46.644 --> 00:03:49.897
Not a stranger to vengeance. are you?

41
00:03:49.897 --> 00:03:53.984
Then you know
it can create unusual allies.

42
00:03:53.984 --> 00:03:55.569
So what did he do to you?

43
00:03:55.569 --> 00:03:57.446
Lovers' quarrel?

44
00:03:57.446 --> 00:04:00.491
It's not what Thordak did.

45
00:04:00.491 --> 00:04:03.077
<i>It's what he didn't do.</i>

46
00:04:04.703 --> 00:04:06.580
<i>Trapped in the Fire Plane.</i>

47
00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.582
<i>tethered to the soul anchor.</i>

48
00:04:08.582 --> 00:04:12.127
<i>Thordak was a pathetic prisoner of flame.</i>

49
00:04:16.006 --> 00:04:20.886
<i>Until I snuck through Pyrah
to strike a deal with him.</i>

50
00:04:20.886 --> 00:04:23.597
<i>A runic curse afflicts me.</i>

51
00:04:23.597 --> 00:04:28.978
<i>But centuries of survival
have given Thordak knowledge of a cure.</i>

52
00:04:28.978 --> 00:04:32.564
Free me. diseased deceiver.

53
00:04:32.564 --> 00:04:35.609
and I shall free you of your ailment.

54
00:04:37.027 --> 00:04:40.531
<i>The bonds of the soul anchor
were unbreakable.</i>

55
00:04:40.531 --> 00:04:42.491
<i>But with my magic.</i>

56
00:04:42.491 --> 00:04:44.243
<i>he gave himself over to it.</i>

57
00:04:44.243 --> 00:04:46.161
<i>Fused with it.</i>

58
00:04:46.161 --> 00:04:49.248
<i>Its elemental force nourishing his body.</i>

59
00:04:49.248 --> 00:04:52.001
<i>contaminating his mind.</i>

60
00:05:01.218 --> 00:05:04.263
<i>I begged him to use prudence.</i>

61
00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:09.852
<i>But the gem gave him ungodly power.</i>

62
00:05:14.773 --> 00:05:17.401
<i>And uncontrollable rage.</i>

63
00:05:23.532 --> 00:05:25.367
He called himself king.

64
00:05:25.367 --> 00:05:27.745
Demanded I find loyal subjects.

65
00:05:27.745 --> 00:05:29.496
His conclave.

66
00:05:30.581 --> 00:05:31.749
And the cure?

67
00:05:31.749 --> 00:05:33.792
There is no cure.

68
00:05:33.792 --> 00:05:35.711
Then why not slay him yourself?

69
00:05:35.711 --> 00:05:38.088
Your magic made him like this.

70
00:05:38.088 --> 00:05:42.051
With that crystal in his chest.
neither of us can destroy him alone.

71
00:05:42.051 --> 00:05:43.302
But together--

72
00:05:43.302 --> 00:05:45.095
There is no "together." bitch.

73
00:05:45.095 --> 00:05:46.722
You opened that rift.

74
00:05:46.722 --> 00:05:49.558
Half of Pyrah is dead because of you.

75
00:05:49.558 --> 00:05:51.727
I freed him. yes.

76
00:05:51.727 --> 00:05:54.229
He massacred your people. true.

77
00:05:54.229 --> 00:05:57.316
I assume you wish me dead. Ashari?

78
00:05:57.316 --> 00:05:58.984
That's an understatement.

79
00:05:58.984 --> 00:06:01.320
Your wish will soon be granted.

80
00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.572
The pain grows worse every day.

81
00:06:03.572 --> 00:06:06.784
But I will see Thordak pay for his lies

82
00:06:06.784 --> 00:06:08.827
before his plan comes to fruition.

83
00:06:08.827 --> 00:06:12.122
Plan. plan-- What plan?
This vague bullshit's getting old.

84
00:06:12.122 --> 00:06:16.877
A new order of elemental dragons
born of his own spawn.

85
00:06:16.877 --> 00:06:20.130
When his brood of eggs in Emon hatches.

86
00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:22.800
your world will be bathed in fire.

87
00:06:28.889 --> 00:06:30.516
My vision.

88
00:06:30.516 --> 00:06:32.559
When will these eggs hatch?

89
00:06:32.559 --> 00:06:34.686
Weeks. Maybe days.

90
00:06:34.686 --> 00:06:38.148
I mean. what are we waitin' for?
We got vesticles--

91
00:06:38.148 --> 00:06:41.193
- Vestiges.
- They whupped Umbrasyl.

92
00:06:41.193 --> 00:06:42.861
Let's charge that castle

93
00:06:42.861 --> 00:06:44.696
- and whup him. too!
- Ha.

94
00:06:44.696 --> 00:06:47.825
You'd be destroyed in a heartbeat.

95
00:06:47.825 --> 00:06:52.371
You may have vestiges
but not the one you need.

96
00:06:52.371 --> 00:06:54.623
The Plate of the Dawnmartyr.

97
00:06:54.623 --> 00:06:58.418
Magical armor
that can repel hellfire itself.

98
00:06:58.418 --> 00:07:00.504
It has felled dragons before.

99
00:07:03.132 --> 00:07:05.551
And it can again.

100
00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:09.805
I don't suppose you brought
this thing with you

101
00:07:09.805 --> 00:07:11.974
in. like. a big purse or. like. a tote?

102
00:07:11.974 --> 00:07:13.851
It resides in Ank'Harel.

103
00:07:13.851 --> 00:07:17.229
Located by Umbrasyl
before you destroyed him.

104
00:07:17.229 --> 00:07:19.815
Now another treasure hunter seeks it.

105
00:07:19.815 --> 00:07:22.151
So time is of the essence.

106
00:07:22.151 --> 00:07:25.320
Raishan. go fuck yourself.

107
00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:27.823
Anyone can conjure illusions.

108
00:07:27.823 --> 00:07:29.366
This is clearly an ambush.

109
00:07:29.366 --> 00:07:31.785
And we are not falling for it.

110
00:07:31.785 --> 00:07:33.328
The answer is no.

111
00:07:33.328 --> 00:07:36.081
You all agree with the Ashari?

112
00:07:36.081 --> 00:07:37.499
We're a team.

113
00:07:40.043 --> 00:07:42.880
Without an alliance. I die.

114
00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:44.715
As do you.

115
00:07:44.715 --> 00:07:48.260
But if that's the path you've chosen--

116
00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:49.636
No. no. don't let her do it.

117
00:07:54.975 --> 00:07:56.185
Kima.

118
00:07:56.185 --> 00:07:57.936
Shaun.

119
00:07:57.936 --> 00:07:59.229
Are you all right?

120
00:07:59.229 --> 00:08:01.231
Waking in your arms again?

121
00:08:01.231 --> 00:08:03.859
Oh. you should start charging me.

122
00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:08.197
Ow.

123
00:08:08.197 --> 00:08:11.116
For the last time. Grog. it's me.

124
00:08:11.116 --> 00:08:13.202
Mm-hmm. Well. then say something

125
00:08:13.202 --> 00:08:16.038
only the real Keeper Yennen would know.

126
00:08:17.122 --> 00:08:20.375
Sometimes you wear a crown
and call yourself

127
00:08:20.375 --> 00:08:23.712
"Grand Poo-bah de Mayonnaise"
when no one's looking.

128
00:08:24.796 --> 00:08:26.506
Yeah. okay. it's her.

129
00:08:26.506 --> 00:08:28.967
Thank the Dawnfather
she only locked you in the dungeon.

130
00:08:28.967 --> 00:08:30.636
It could have been far worse.

131
00:08:30.636 --> 00:08:32.221
The question remains.

132
00:08:32.221 --> 00:08:34.848
Do we dare chase down this armor?

133
00:08:34.848 --> 00:08:36.433
Conspire with Raishan?

134
00:08:36.433 --> 00:08:37.851
No way.

135
00:08:37.851 --> 00:08:39.645
She killed Sovereign Uriel.

136
00:08:39.645 --> 00:08:41.021
It's a deal with a devil.

137
00:08:41.021 --> 00:08:42.522
But how badass would it be

138
00:08:42.522 --> 00:08:45.067
if we rolled in riding a fucking dragon?

139
00:08:45.067 --> 00:08:47.486
Knock-knock. Thordak! Acid!

140
00:08:47.486 --> 00:08:48.904
Uh. she shoots poison.

141
00:08:48.904 --> 00:08:49.988
Oh. Right.

142
00:08:49.988 --> 00:08:51.657
Knock-knock. Thordak!

143
00:08:51.657 --> 00:08:53.242
Poison!

144
00:08:53.242 --> 00:08:56.078
If she helps defeat the conclave.
that's well worth it.

145
00:08:56.078 --> 00:08:59.957
I don't like this. either.
but Raishan could have just attacked us.

146
00:08:59.957 --> 00:09:01.792
She wanted to talk.

147
00:09:01.792 --> 00:09:03.377
Maybe we should listen.

148
00:09:03.377 --> 00:09:05.003
To a mass murderer?

149
00:09:05.003 --> 00:09:08.799
Sometimes a stiff moral code
must be bent for the greater good.

150
00:09:08.799 --> 00:09:09.883
No!

151
00:09:09.883 --> 00:09:12.678
I will not dishonor the Ashari.

152
00:09:16.848 --> 00:09:19.476
I'll go after her.

153
00:09:21.937 --> 00:09:24.356
So. we all going out the window?

154
00:09:34.116 --> 00:09:35.617
Whoever's there.

155
00:09:35.617 --> 00:09:37.869
you don't want to fuck with me tonight.

156
00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.497
I don't doubt it.

157
00:09:42.916 --> 00:09:47.004
The idea of working with that monster.

158
00:09:47.004 --> 00:09:48.672
After what she did to my people.

159
00:09:48.672 --> 00:09:49.756
I know.

160
00:09:49.756 --> 00:09:53.260
And the rest of the team.

161
00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:55.804
It always feels like
my opinions don't count.

162
00:09:55.804 --> 00:09:57.347
They count with me.

163
00:09:57.347 --> 00:09:59.057
Do they. Vax?

164
00:09:59.057 --> 00:10:01.810
Y-You've been so...

165
00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:03.061
different.

166
00:10:03.061 --> 00:10:04.479
I miss you.

167
00:10:04.479 --> 00:10:07.691
There were things I needed to understand.

168
00:10:07.691 --> 00:10:08.859
With the Matron.

169
00:10:08.859 --> 00:10:10.527
And do you?

170
00:10:11.611 --> 00:10:14.573
Not everything. But enough.

171
00:10:14.573 --> 00:10:16.450
There's a balance.

172
00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:19.161
Like I'm finally ready for...

173
00:10:19.161 --> 00:10:21.330
whatever comes next.

174
00:10:25.125 --> 00:10:28.045
I'm glad you have someone
who supports you.

175
00:10:28.045 --> 00:10:30.589
Kiki.

176
00:10:31.798 --> 00:10:34.384
I can be that person for you.

177
00:10:34.384 --> 00:10:35.969
if you need me to.

178
00:10:37.804 --> 00:10:41.308
I need that a lot right now.

179
00:11:04.748 --> 00:11:07.084
Sorry. Sorry. Was that bad?

180
00:11:07.084 --> 00:11:09.044
I-I felt your tongue.
and it freaked me out.

181
00:11:09.044 --> 00:11:11.838
and-and I'm-I'm new at this and--

182
00:11:11.838 --> 00:11:15.592
No. no. it was wonderful.

183
00:11:15.592 --> 00:11:18.720
Just... intense.

184
00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:22.140
And. um. I-I need a moment.

185
00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:24.184
Oh. um. okay.

186
00:11:24.184 --> 00:11:26.812
I'll walk back first. then.

187
00:11:26.812 --> 00:11:28.897
so no one suspects.

188
00:11:28.897 --> 00:11:30.857
I'll see you there.

189
00:11:41.368 --> 00:11:43.120
You're up early.

190
00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:45.664
Never slept. I hate our options.

191
00:11:45.664 --> 00:11:49.334
And I hate how it's driving a wedge
between the group.

192
00:11:49.334 --> 00:11:51.253
Bollocks.

193
00:11:51.253 --> 00:11:54.172
What's really bothering you. darling?

194
00:11:56.341 --> 00:11:59.261
When the Briarwoods came.

195
00:11:59.261 --> 00:12:01.763
no one could have prevented it.

196
00:12:01.763 --> 00:12:04.850
But this... I did this.

197
00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:09.020
I had us flee here. and Raishan followed.

198
00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:11.523
I've endangered my people once more.

199
00:12:11.523 --> 00:12:15.110
The way you self-analyze.
I've always admired it.

200
00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:18.613
But at some point.
you have to forgive yourself.

201
00:12:18.613 --> 00:12:20.949
No one can undo the past.

202
00:12:20.949 --> 00:12:23.285
Well. one can certainly try.

203
00:12:24.286 --> 00:12:27.164
You may know me better
than I know myself. Vex'ahlia.

204
00:12:27.164 --> 00:12:31.751
And you're right. I must focus
on the problems ahead.

205
00:12:31.751 --> 00:12:33.920
On fixing this.

206
00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:35.589
Well. not this. This is rubbish.

207
00:12:35.589 --> 00:12:38.341
I know we can.

208
00:12:38.341 --> 00:12:40.051
Together.

209
00:12:42.095 --> 00:12:44.097
Hmm.

210
00:12:45.807 --> 00:12:47.934
Right.

211
00:12:47.934 --> 00:12:51.771
I was thinking. it won't matter
whether Raishan is lying

212
00:12:51.771 --> 00:12:53.940
if we can get to those eggs.

213
00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:57.277
If they're real. we'd have an ally.

214
00:12:57.277 --> 00:12:58.528
And if they aren't--

215
00:12:58.528 --> 00:13:01.406
Then we let our vestiges do the talking.

216
00:13:01.406 --> 00:13:03.700
Shall we wake the others?

217
00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:05.994
Trinket?

218
00:13:11.291 --> 00:13:15.212
Sun Tree. if you can hear me.
grant us luck.

219
00:13:20.842 --> 00:13:23.678
A stealth mission
into a dragon's lair.

220
00:13:23.678 --> 00:13:26.640
You've come a long way
from stealing from my shop.

221
00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:28.725
my handsome half-elf.

222
00:13:28.725 --> 00:13:31.937
Ah. you know. Same game. bigger walls.

223
00:13:31.937 --> 00:13:33.980
The item you requested.

224
00:13:35.065 --> 00:13:36.525
Should make quite a show.

225
00:13:36.525 --> 00:13:39.194
I'd expect nothing less. Shaun.

226
00:13:39.194 --> 00:13:41.029
This feels weird every time.

227
00:13:41.029 --> 00:13:43.365
Hmm.

228
00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:53.792
Whoa. Place looks like shit.

229
00:13:55.877 --> 00:13:58.255
Good to be home.

230
00:14:01.299 --> 00:14:03.176
All right. huddle up.

231
00:14:03.176 --> 00:14:07.138
As we know. I'll be making
a daring aerial incursion.

232
00:14:07.138 --> 00:14:08.640
Which is certain to fail.

233
00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:10.308
I mean. I wouldn't say "certain."

234
00:14:10.308 --> 00:14:12.644
Is highly likely to fail.

235
00:14:12.644 --> 00:14:15.063
I'm sort of with Vex on this one.

236
00:14:16.147 --> 00:14:17.774
Thank you. Stubby.

237
00:14:17.774 --> 00:14:20.527
In any case. you all have
your backup assignments.

238
00:14:20.527 --> 00:14:21.736
Yep.

239
00:14:21.736 --> 00:14:23.947
<i>I'm on rock duty.</i>

240
00:14:23.947 --> 00:14:26.950
<i>Me and Grog will get
up close and personal with our vestiges.</i>

241
00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:28.118
<i>Vesticles.</i>

242
00:14:28.118 --> 00:14:30.120
<i>With mine circling overhead.</i>

243
00:14:31.246 --> 00:14:32.581
<i>I'll be watching Vax.</i>

244
00:14:32.581 --> 00:14:35.667
<i>And I'll be ready
with the signal for when he fails.</i>

245
00:14:35.667 --> 00:14:38.461
If. If I fail.

246
00:14:38.461 --> 00:14:40.297
Sure. brother. Sure.

247
00:14:41.339 --> 00:14:43.592
Plan sounds aces.

248
00:14:43.592 --> 00:14:45.677
What could possibly go wrong?

249
00:14:51.725 --> 00:14:53.810
No!

250
00:15:09.326 --> 00:15:11.161
Shit. shit. Do the thing!

251
00:15:19.377 --> 00:15:22.172
Let's give him a taste of our toys!

252
00:15:24.341 --> 00:15:26.885
<i>♪ Mythcarver ho! ♪</i>

253
00:15:26.885 --> 00:15:28.928
More insects.

254
00:15:28.928 --> 00:15:31.681
Oh. fuck!

255
00:15:35.435 --> 00:15:38.104
A bigger target.

256
00:16:02.212 --> 00:16:03.922
Oi! Thordak!

257
00:16:12.764 --> 00:16:15.225
Come on. We need to rejoin the fight.

258
00:16:15.225 --> 00:16:16.851
No. damn it.

259
00:16:16.851 --> 00:16:18.687
She was right about all of it.

260
00:16:18.687 --> 00:16:20.397
The eggs. the nest.

261
00:16:20.397 --> 00:16:22.482
The vestiges aren't enough.

262
00:16:22.482 --> 00:16:24.234
We need to run.

263
00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:38.707
These are the vestiges
Umbrasyl coveted?

264
00:16:38.707 --> 00:16:43.294
Your relics will lie in ash
with your corpses.

265
00:16:45.046 --> 00:16:46.673
Go! Take cover!

266
00:16:54.764 --> 00:16:55.849
Pike!

267
00:17:03.106 --> 00:17:05.275
We need to hide! Now!

268
00:17:07.277 --> 00:17:08.695
Quickly! In there!

269
00:17:19.664 --> 00:17:21.833
Can't run. can't hide. What do we do?

270
00:17:21.833 --> 00:17:23.251
The arrogance!

271
00:17:23.251 --> 00:17:26.463
That you would dare enter my domain?

272
00:17:32.385 --> 00:17:35.764
- Raishan?
- Careful where you point that.

273
00:17:35.764 --> 00:17:37.265
This is your fault.

274
00:17:37.265 --> 00:17:38.808
You told Thordak we were coming.

275
00:17:38.808 --> 00:17:41.394
Fool. I warned you.

276
00:17:41.394 --> 00:17:44.439
Get us out of here. and we'll reconsider.

277
00:17:44.439 --> 00:17:46.566
Finally. a rational mind.

278
00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:54.491
Come close.

279
00:17:55.867 --> 00:17:57.535
Group hug. Everybody get intimate.

280
00:18:14.511 --> 00:18:16.513
Somebody put out that fire.

281
00:18:16.513 --> 00:18:18.139
I gotcha. Just-- Aah!

282
00:18:19.432 --> 00:18:21.142
Kiki...

283
00:18:28.441 --> 00:18:30.902
Hold still. Try not to move.

284
00:18:33.321 --> 00:18:34.948
Now do you trust me?

285
00:18:37.742 --> 00:18:39.869
Then make haste for Ank'Harel.

286
00:18:51.047 --> 00:18:53.466
You're safe. my progeny.

287
00:18:53.466 --> 00:18:55.093
Safe.

288
00:18:55.093 --> 00:18:56.761
But how did they get that close?

289
00:18:58.555 --> 00:19:00.849
No. it's all right. Shh.

290
00:19:00.849 --> 00:19:02.725
It won't happen again.

291
00:19:02.725 --> 00:19:06.229
For I will have Vox Machina brought to me.

292
00:19:06.229 --> 00:19:10.400
and they shall burn.

293
00:19:38.344 --> 00:19:41.014
{\an8}Ank'Harel. the Jewel of Marquet.

294
00:19:41.014 --> 00:19:44.058
{\an8}Also. fun fact. my old stomping grounds.

295
00:19:44.058 --> 00:19:47.353
Over here is the famed Suncut Bazaar.

296
00:19:47.353 --> 00:19:50.356
The River District. where you can find
anything your heart desires.

297
00:19:50.356 --> 00:19:51.816
And I do mean anything.

298
00:19:52.901 --> 00:19:54.068
<i>Ah.</i>

299
00:19:54.068 --> 00:19:57.322
<i>Those fearsome men in uniform
are the Hand of Ord.</i>

300
00:19:57.322 --> 00:20:02.160
<i>Guardians of the mysterious emperex
of this place. J'mon Sa Ord.</i>

301
00:20:04.454 --> 00:20:07.415
<i>And down this street is where
your dragon friend said</i>

302
00:20:07.415 --> 00:20:09.918
<i>we'd find the vestige.</i>

303
00:20:09.918 --> 00:20:14.130
I. uh. don't suppose you want to break in
and steal a priceless relic for us?

304
00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:16.966
Mm. I'm a salesman now. friend.

305
00:20:16.966 --> 00:20:20.261
All your palace intrigue.
no longer intriguing.

306
00:20:20.261 --> 00:20:24.223
If you need me. I'll be sipping
a glass of Stassman down the street.

307
00:20:24.223 --> 00:20:25.516
Ta-ta.

308
00:20:25.516 --> 00:20:27.727
Hey. uh. Gil. if a fella were looking for

309
00:20:27.727 --> 00:20:29.854
a traveling musical act around here.

310
00:20:29.854 --> 00:20:31.648
where would he start?

311
00:20:31.648 --> 00:20:33.775
Where do you think you're going?

312
00:20:33.775 --> 00:20:36.945
Vex. remember that favor you owe me?

313
00:20:40.031 --> 00:20:41.574
All right. we know the drill.

314
00:20:41.574 --> 00:20:43.660
Simple smash-and-grab. Home by supper.

315
00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:45.328
Easier said than done.

316
00:20:45.328 --> 00:20:47.747
It's high noon. There are eyes everywhere.

317
00:20:47.747 --> 00:20:49.707
Then we call it off.

318
00:20:49.707 --> 00:20:51.376
What?

319
00:20:51.376 --> 00:20:54.879
Raishan's holding all the cards.
and we're exactly where she wants us.

320
00:20:55.964 --> 00:20:57.715
Vax?

321
00:20:57.715 --> 00:21:00.301
What other play do we have?

322
00:21:00.301 --> 00:21:02.178
I-I don't know.

323
00:21:02.178 --> 00:21:04.555
But I refuse to believe
that our only two choices

324
00:21:04.555 --> 00:21:06.182
are Raishan or failure.

325
00:21:06.182 --> 00:21:08.434
Keyleth. I--

326
00:21:09.727 --> 00:21:12.772
Percy? That sounded like...

327
00:21:36.379 --> 00:21:39.716
We're not the only ones
who want that plate.

328
00:21:43.261 --> 00:21:44.595
These wounds.

329
00:21:44.595 --> 00:21:47.807
Hey. Stay with me. Who did this to you?

330
00:21:47.807 --> 00:21:51.102
She is still here.

331
00:22:04.032 --> 00:22:06.743
A pepperbox. It can't be.

332
00:22:06.743 --> 00:22:09.662
Percy. we need to keep our heads
if we're going to--

333
00:22:09.662 --> 00:22:11.789
- Right behind you. Percy!
- Wait!

334
00:22:33.728 --> 00:22:35.980
Everyone. get down!

335
00:22:40.151 --> 00:22:41.402
Sorry.

336
00:22:41.402 --> 00:22:42.737
I'll try to stabilize him.

337
00:22:44.155 --> 00:22:46.449
Vex. your broom. Follow them.

338
00:22:46.449 --> 00:22:48.993
I... I gave it to Scanlan.

339
00:22:48.993 --> 00:22:50.161
You what?!

340
00:23:18.439 --> 00:23:20.858
Vax. look out!

341
00:23:20.858 --> 00:23:22.610
Ah. shit. Sorry.

342
00:23:51.514 --> 00:23:52.598
Spice?

343
00:23:52.598 --> 00:23:53.975
Aah! Uh. I'm sorry. what?

344
00:23:53.975 --> 00:23:56.352
You spice? Spice it?

345
00:23:56.352 --> 00:23:57.770
What? Oh.

346
00:23:57.770 --> 00:23:59.438
Uh. I mean. sometime--

347
00:23:59.438 --> 00:24:01.774
No. no. not right now. I'm--

348
00:24:01.774 --> 00:24:03.234
I'm going to see my daughter.

349
00:24:03.234 --> 00:24:05.361
Oh.

350
00:24:05.361 --> 00:24:07.029
Does she spice?

351
00:24:08.072 --> 00:24:09.323
Dude.

352
00:24:12.451 --> 00:24:13.911
Huh?

353
00:24:27.633 --> 00:24:30.094
Dr. Anna Ripley.

354
00:24:31.596 --> 00:24:34.015
Why am I not surprised. Percival?

355
00:24:34.015 --> 00:24:37.226
Then again. you put things together
faster than anyone I've met.

356
00:24:37.226 --> 00:24:40.688
Hand over the vestige.
and I may let you live.

357
00:24:40.688 --> 00:24:42.732
Which one?

358
00:24:44.317 --> 00:24:47.653
Mythcarver was quite handy
before you stole it back.

359
00:24:48.654 --> 00:24:52.408
Ah. you've improved my old prototype.

360
00:24:52.408 --> 00:24:53.701
How flattering.

361
00:24:53.701 --> 00:24:55.661
There's nowhere to run. Ripley.

362
00:24:55.661 --> 00:24:57.413
You're all alone.

363
00:24:57.413 --> 00:24:59.832
Oh. that's the thing. Percival.

364
00:24:59.832 --> 00:25:02.793
I'm never alone.

365
00:25:08.341 --> 00:25:11.677
We had a bargain. Percy.

366
00:25:11.677 --> 00:25:15.765
And I will happily collect.

367
00:25:40.289 --> 00:25:42.375
<i>♪ Do ya spice? ♪</i>

368
00:25:42.375 --> 00:25:46.212
<i>♪ Oh. ah. gotcha. unh! ♪</i>

369
00:25:46.212 --> 00:25:48.464
<i>♪ You wanna spice? ♪</i>

370
00:25:48.464 --> 00:25:50.716
<i>♪ Sexy mama ♪</i>

371
00:25:50.716 --> 00:25:53.844
<i>♪ Oh. get nice with me and spice ♪</i>

372
00:26:15.324 --> 00:26:17.285
Chirp.

372
